  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>First step of the reaction involves acid base reaction to form&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>Bu</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><msup><mi>Li</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>.This is due to the presence of acidic hydrogen in the reactant Hex-1-yne.</p><p>Second step involves nucleophilic substitution to form a higher alkyne.</p><p>Third step involves hydrogenation of alkyne&nbsp;by using lindlar catalyst to form cis-alkene</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/782bde96-815c-48bb-979f-5e0291b67cbb-73d5ed69-7dd9-418f-9390-b25328f435d2-image.png\" style=\"width: 528px; height: 239px;\" /></p>",
